### Demo data: mvn quarkus:dev
### or Docker: orgkeep-compose, docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml -f docker-compose.demo.yaml up -d
### Accounts (realm "demo"): realm-owner / password, org-owner / password (owner of the organisation "acme")
### Tokens: login client of the realm (clientId = realm name), password grant enabled for the demo by DemoSeeder

### Token of the realm owner
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=realm-owner
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password

> {%
    client.global.set("realm_owner_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Token of the owner of acme
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=org-owner
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password

> {%
    client.global.set("org_owner_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Token of org-user (Claire): the default catalog "products" is a default scope of the login client,
### resource_access.products has billing, given by the team users
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=org-user
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password

### Token of paul, team ops, catalog prod only: resource_access.prod, pools acme and acme/ops in the claim "prod"
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=paul
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password
    &scope=openid prod

### Token of paul, catalog sandbox only: the API of prod refuses it (prod is not in aud)
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=paul
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password
    &scope=openid sandbox

### Realm owner: list organisations
GET http://localhost:8282/api/admin/organisations
Authorization: Bearer {{realm_owner_token}}

### Org owner: list the members of acme
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/members
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: add a member to acme
POST http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/members
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@acme.test",
  "firstName": "Bob",
  "lastName": "Smith"
}

### Org owner: the teams of acme, with what they give
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/user-groups
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: the products of acme, to configure the teams
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/products
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: the team analysts gives legal-repository in prod, scan only, with a quota of team (cycle of the org)
PUT http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/user-groups/analysts/products/prod/legal-repository
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "features": ["scan"],
  "quota": 200
}

### Org owner: the catalog roles of prod the teams can give
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/catalogs/prod/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: forbidden on the realm owner endpoints (403)
GET http://localhost:8282/api/admin/organisations
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}
